Message(id='msg_01A242DLFYhrcbiSatYQKf5o', container=None, content=[TextBlock(citations=None, text='Here is a clear summary of each file:\n\n---\n\n## 📁 File Summaries\n\n---\n\n### `s01_agent_loop.py` — **The Core Agent Loop**\n> *"The entire secret of an AI coding agent in one pattern."*\n\nThis is the **foundation** of the series. It implements the simplest possible agentic loop:\n- **Single tool:** `bash` — runs shell commands via `subprocess`.\n- **The loop:** Repeatedly calls the Anthropic LLM (`claude`), appends its response to a message history, executes any `bash` tool calls it makes, feeds the results back in, and repeats — **until the model stops requesting tools**.\n- **Safety:** Blocks a small set of dangerous commands (e.g., `rm -rf /`, `sudo`).\n- **Interface:** An interactive REPL (`s01 >>`) where users type tasks and the agent autonomously executes shell commands to solve them.\n\n**Key Insight:** The entire agent pattern is a `while stop_reason == "tool_use":` loop.\n\n---\n\n### `s02_tool_use.py` — **Expanded Tool Dispatch**\n> *"The loop didn\'t change at all. I just added tools."*\n\nBuilds directly on `s01` by **adding more tools** while keeping the same loop structure:\n- **Four tools:** `bash`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file` — giving the agent full file system access (reading, writing, and surgical text replacement).\n- **Tool Dispatch Map:** Introduces a `TOOL_HANDLERS` dictionary `{tool_name: handler_fn}` to cleanly route any tool call the model makes to the correct Python function.\n- **Workspace safety:** A `safe_path()` guard ensures all file operations stay within the working directory (no path traversal).\n- **Interface:** Same interactive REPL pattern (`s02 >>`).\n\n**Key Insight:** Expanding agent capability is purely additive — add a handler function, add the tool schema to the list, done. The loop is untouched.\n\n---\n\n### `s03_todo_write.py` — **Self-Tracking with TodoWrite**\n> *"The agent can track its own progress — and I can see it."*\n\nBuilds on `s02` by adding a **planning/progress-tracking layer**:\n- **New `todo` tool:** The LLM writes and updates a structured task list (`TodoManager`) with statuses: `pending`, `in_progress`, and `completed`. Only one task can be `in_progress` at a time (enforced by validation).\n- **Nag Reminder Injection:** If the model goes **3+ rounds without updating its todos**, a `<reminder>` message is automatically injected into the next tool result, escalating in urgency over time. This keeps the agent on track for long, multi-step tasks.\n- **Extended Thinking:** Enables Anthropic\'s "thinking" feature (`budget_tokens: 10000`) to let the model reason more deeply before acting.\n- **Interface:** Same REPL pattern (`s03 >>`).\n\n**Key Insight:** The agent can maintain observable, structured state about its own plan — and the harness can nudge it back on track when it drifts.\n\n---\n\n### `s04_subagent.py` — **Subagent / Context Isolation**\n> *"Process isolation gives context isolation for free."*\n\nThe most advanced pattern, introducing **parent/child agent delegation**:\n- **New `task` tool (parent only):** The parent agent can spawn a **subagent** by calling `task(prompt=..., description=...)`. The subagent runs in a completely **fresh message history** (`messages=[]`), does its work (using all base tools), and returns only a **text summary** to the parent.\n- **Context isolation:** The subagent\'s full tool-call history and intermediate steps are **discarded** after it finishes — only the final summary bubbles back up. This prevents the parent\'s context from being polluted by a subagent\'s verbose working.\n- **Shared filesystem:** Both parent and child operate on the same working directory, so the subagent\'s file changes are visible to the parent.\n- **No recursive spawning:** The child does NOT have the `task` tool, preventing infinite agent nesting.\n- **Safety limit:** The subagent loop caps at 30 iterations.\n\n**Key Insight:** Delegating work to a subagent with a clean context window keeps the parent focused and prevents context bloat on long, complex tasks.\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Progression Summary\n\n| File | Core Concept | New Addition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `s01` | Agent Loop | `bash` tool + `while tool_use` loop |\n| `s02` | Tool Dispatch | `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file` + dispatch map |\n| `s03` | Planning | `todo` tool + nag reminder injection |\n| `s04` | Subagents | `task` tool + fresh-context child agents |\n\nEach file is a **self-contained, runnable learning step**, building one concept at a time on top of the last, forming a complete curriculum for understanding how production AI coding agents are structured.', type='text')], model='claude-sonnet-4-6', role='assistant', stop_details=None, stop_reason='end_turn', stop_sequence=None, type='message', usage=Usage(cache_creation=CacheCreation(ephemeral_1h_input_tokens=0, ephemeral_5m_input_tokens=0), cache_creation_input_tokens=0, cache_read_input_tokens=0, inference_geo='global', input_tokens=9704, output_tokens=1216, server_tool_use=None, service_tier='standard'))
